# Pontia documentation

Pontia turns your device into an agent cloud. Coding agents run with the tools and project files on your device while you monitor and control their sessions from a local or remote dashboard.

## Start here

- [Getting started](/docs/getting-started) — install Pontia, choose your agent integrations, and initialize the local service.
- [How Pontia works](/docs/how-it-works) — understand local execution, remote connectivity, and the boundaries between your device, Pontia Cloud, and Edge.
- [Remote access](/docs/remote-access) — sign in, register your device, and control its agent sessions from the web.

## How Pontia works

Agent execution stays on your device. Pontia runs a local service that manages sessions and serves the local dashboard. When remote access is enabled, the public dashboard connects through an official or self-hosted Edge.

Traffic between the remote dashboard and your device is encrypted end to end. The Edge provides connectivity and relays ciphertext; it does not run your agents or hold your project files.
